EXT. HEDGE MAZE - WEDDING VENUE - AFTERNOON

Eight-foot yew walls. Gravel paths. A white tent glimpsed over the green. A string quartet drifts in from somewhere unseen.

PRUDENCE "PRU" SHETTY (30s, bridesmaid in sage satin, flats in her hand) strides down a corridor of hedge, scanning left and right.

PRU
Joaquín? Joaquín!

She reaches a fork. A pair of legs in tuxedo trousers sticks out from under a bench at the end of a dead-end.

JOAQUÍN SANTANA-REYES (30s, groom, tie undone, a flask in his fist) is lying there, staring at the underside of the bench.

PRU (CONT'D)
You are forty minutes late to your own wedding.

JOAQUÍN
I'm not late. I'm lost.

PRU
It's the same thing with a bow tie.

She drops to her knees beside him. He offers the flask. She takes a swig and grimaces.

PRU (CONT'D)
That's cough syrup.

JOAQUÍN
It was all I could find.

Gravel crunches. ODALYS FONTENOT (20s, bride, veil pinned to her wrist like a bracelet, running shoes under the gown) rounds the corner and halts.

ODALYS
There you are.

JOAQUÍN
Odalys.

ODALYS
I've been through this maze eleven times.

PRU
Eleven?

ODALYS
Well, nine. Two were the same dead end.

JOAQUÍN
I can't remember the vows.

ODALYS
I wrote them down.

JOAQUÍN
I lost the card.

ODALYS
I have a copy.

PRU
(over her)
Jo, breathe.

JOAQUÍN
(over Pru)
I'm breathing.

ODALYS
(over both)
You are not breathing, you're panicking, which is different, and it's adorable.

A new voice, deep and calm, cuts in from behind the hedge.

OFFICIANT DESMOND VANTERPOOL (60s, black robe, rain boots) strides around the corner with a clipboard, a walkie-talkie squawking at his belt.

DESMOND
Found them. Both of them. And the maid of honor.

PRU
Bridesmaid.

DESMOND
Bridesmaid. Of course.

A FLOWER GIRL, TILLY BRANDT (7, petals in her fist, grass-stained knees), skids in behind him and points at everyone in turn.

TILLY
Is this the wedding?

DESMOND
It's the pre-wedding.

He looks at the four of them in the gravel. He checks his watch.

DESMOND (CONT'D)
The guests are on their third appetizer. I can do this right here, if you'd like.

JOAQUÍN
Here?

DESMOND
There's a bench.

ODALYS
Pru, hold the veil.

PRU
I'm the witness?

ODALYS
You're the witness.

Joaquín scrambles out from under the bench. Odalys takes his hands. Desmond opens a small book. Pru, still holding her shoes, raises one in the air like a toast.

DESMOND
Dearly beloved, and also hedge.
